  "name": null,
  "problem": "If ${X}_{1}∼N(2,3)$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(7,25)$ are independent and $Y=5{X}_{1}-{X}_{2},$ calculate $P(Y>20).$ Round your final answer to two decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9332\\,$ | $\\,0.9345\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ | $\\,0.9370\\,$ | $\\,0.9382\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9452\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ | $\\,0.9484\\,$ | $\\,0.9495\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9554\\,$ | $\\,0.9564\\,$ | $\\,0.9573\\,$ | $\\,0.9582\\,$ | $\\,0.9591\\,$ |",
